<!-----------------------BEGIN SIDEBAR-----------------------
 
Now I'm going to show you how to edit these filters!
 
IMPORTANT:
 
dont touch <button class="button is-checked" data-filter="">all</button> anywhere. It makes sure that you can reset the categories. You can change "all" to whatever you want (reset, show all, etc.) just don't delete it completely.
 
 
 
HOW TO CHANGE THE FILTERS: -------------------------
 
It's actually easier than you think! Lets say you're making a clique rp.
All you have to do is change category one to something like this:
 
    <button class="button" data-filter=".jocks">jocks</button>
    <button class="button" data-filter=".populars">populars</button>
    <button class="button" data-filter=".nerds">nerds</button>
    <button class="button" data-filter=".theatre">theatre geeks</button>
 
   Notice how for the theatre geeks one, they don't match? They don't have to match! Check out the original character and canon character labels in category three. They're oc and cc respectively. You can use shortcuts to label your characters because the only thing that shows is the text outside of the < >. If you wanted to, you could actually keep the filter names and just change it to something like
 
    <button class="button" data-filter=".une">jocks</button>
    <button class="button" data-filter=".deux">populars</button>
    <button class="button" data-filter=".trois">nerds</button>
    <button class="button" data-filter=".quatre">theatre geeks</button> 
 
ADDING MORE FILTERS: ---------------------------------
 
Also easy once you get the hang of it! Copy the last button and just past some after like so
 
    <button class="button" data-filter=".jocks">jocks</button>
    <button class="button" data-filter=".populars">populars</button>
    <button class="button" data-filter=".nerds">nerds</button>
    <button class="button" data-filter=".theatre">theatre geeks</button>
    <button class="button" data-filter=".theatre">theatre geeks</button>
    <button class="button" data-filter=".theatre">theatre geeks</button>
    <button class="button" data-filter=".theatre">theatre geeks</button>
 
then change them to whatever you want!    
 
 
HOW TO ADD ANOTHER GROUP:--------------------------------
 
lets say you've done all the steps above to organize your clique rp by clique, avaliability and character type, but you also want to organize them by grade. What you'd do is copy the last category and paste it under.
 
 <!-- category three ->
    <div class="button-group" data-filter-group="type">
        <h1>CHARACTER TYPE</h1>
        <button class="button is-checked" data-filter="">all</button>
        <button class="button" data-filter=".cc">canon character </button>
        <button class="button" data-filter=".oc">original character</button>
        <button class="button" data-filter=".wanted">most wanted</button>
    </div>
 
 <!-- category three ->
    <div class="button-group" data-filter-group="type">
        <h1>CHARACTER TYPE</h1>
        <button class="button is-checked" data-filter="">all</button>
        <button class="button" data-filter=".cc">canon character </button>
        <button class="button" data-filter=".oc">original character</button>
        <button class="button" data-filter=".wanted">most wanted</button>
    </div>    
 
Now you'd change those to whatever you want like we did above! Make sure you change "type" in data-filter-group="type" to something else too.
 
EXAMPLE WITH EVERYTHING CHANGED:
 
 
